amblyopia,AMBLYOPIA,A. Amblyopia or decreased distant vision which meets all the following: • Simple Refractive or Strabismic • One eye only • Unaffected eye Distance Vision is 20/20 or better (for all classes) Decreased vision caused by a process strictly limited to one eye with a fully normal fellow eye and an onset consistent with developmental adaptation,"Submit the following for FAA review: - 1. Amblyopia Status Summary OR a current, detailed Clinical Progress Note generated from a clinic visit with their treating ophthalmologist or optometrist no more than 90 days before the AME exam which addresses all items on the Status Summary. - 2. Any associated progress notes.","DEFER Summarize findings in Item 60. Submit the information to the FAA. In Item 60, specify the airman’s preferred FSDO if a Medical Flight Test (MFT) is required.","<p><strong>A</strong>. Amblyopia or decreased distant vision which meets all the following:</p>
