amblyopia-lazy-eye-status-summary-developmental-adaptation-to-unilateral-visual,Amblyopia (Lazy Eye) Status Summary (Developmental adaptation to unilateral visual impairment*),A. Cataract(s) present; The individual meets the vision standards for class applied; and quality of vision is not affected: For more information see Pilot Vision,If the AME can determine the condition is under control and vision meets standards with no symptoms that would interfere with flight or safety-related duties such as: - Glare - Halos - Loss of contrast sensitivity - Poor night vision,"ISSUE Annotate Block 60. If correction was needed to meet standards, apply Limitation 102 to certificate. Warn the pilot CFR 61.53 applies if any change or worsening in vision.","<p><strong>A. </strong></p>
