coronary-heart-disease,CORONARY HEART DISEASE,B. Cause of angina or chest pain NOT Identified or uncertain in medical records.,"Submit the following for FAA review: 1. Hospital records to include: - Admission history & physical (H&P) - Discharge summary from the physician (NOT the discharge instructions/paperwork given to the patient when leaving the hospital). 2. Coronary catheterization/ angiography report (if performed). 3. Current, detailed Clinical Progress Note(s) from any follow-up visits. It must specifically include the diagnosis and whether it was cardiac in nature or other. If cardiac, additional evaluation may be required. 4. Any other testing already performed for this condition. If no cause is identified, additional information may be required.",DEFER Submit the information to the FAA for a possible Special Issuance. Annotate (elements or findings) in Block 60.,<p><strong>B. </strong>Cause of angina or chest pain NOT Identified or uncertain in medical records.</p>,"<p>Submit the following for FAA review:</p>
<p>1. Hospital records to include:</p>
<ul><li>Admission history &amp; physical (H&amp;P)</li><li>Discharge summary from the physician (NOT the discharge instructions/paperwork given to the patient when leaving the hospital).</li></ul>
<p>2. Coronary catheterization/ angiography report (if performed).</p>
<p>3. Current, detailed Clinical Progress Note(s) from any follow-up visits. It must specifically include the diagnosis and whether it was cardiac in nature or other. <strong>If cardiac, additional evaluation may be required.</strong></p>
<p>4. Any other testing already performed for this condition.</p>
<p>If no cause is identified, additional information may be required.</p>","<p><strong>DEFER </strong></p>
<p>Submit the information to the FAA for a possible Special Issuance.</p>
<p>Annotate (elements or findings) in Block 60.</p>"
