<p>Submit the information to the FAA for a possible Special Issuance.</p>
<p>Follow up Issuance</p>
<p>Will be per the airman’s authorization letter</p>"
coronary-heart-disease,CORONARY HEART DISEASE,"A. Simple, known cause* (e.g., blood draw) AND Completely resolved *May be single or multiple events from known cause.","The AME should gather information regarding the diagnosis, severity, treatment, symptoms, and address ALL of the questions on the Syncope Decision Tool for the AME. If an underlying cause if found, or if from head injury or associated with drugs or alcohol, see that section.","If ALL items on the Syncope Decision Tool are in the “NO”/clear column, the AME may: ISSUE Summarize this history and annotate Block 60 with “Discussed the history of SYNCOPE, no positives to screening questions, and no concerns.” If any “YES” answers, any AME concerns, or unable to verify history - go to Row B.","<p><strong>A.</strong></p>
<p>Simple, <strong>known</strong> cause*</p>
<p>(e.g., blood draw)</p>
<p>AND</p>
<p><strong>Completely</strong> resolved</p>
<p>*May be single or multiple events from <strong>known</strong> cause.</p>","<p>The AME should gather information regarding the diagnosis, severity, treatment, symptoms, and address <strong>ALL </strong>of the questions on the <a href=""https://www.faa.gov/ame_guide/media/Syncope_Decision_Tool.pdf"" target=""_blank"" rel=""noopener"">Syncope Decision Tool for the AME.</a></p>
<p>If an underlying cause if found, or if from head injury or associated with drugs or alcohol, see that section.</p>","<p>If <strong>ALL</strong> items on the Syncope Decision Tool are in the<strong> “NO”/clear column, the AME may: </strong></p>
<p><strong>ISSUE </strong></p>
<p>Summarize this history and annotate Block 60 with <strong>“Discussed the history of SYNCOPE, no positives to screening questions, and no concerns.” </strong></p>
<p>If any “<strong>YES</strong>” answers, any AME concerns,</p>
<p>or unable to verify history - go to Row B.</p>"
coronary-heart-disease,CORONARY HEART DISEASE,"B. Unknown or unexplained cause OR Multiple unrelated syncopal events If due to a cardiac cause such as myocardial infarction or ischemia, see that page","Submit the following for FAA review: Testing must be performed within the past 90 days to be considered current. - Cardiac Evaluation ; - Echocardiogram (Echo); - Exercise Stress Test (EST); - 14-day Holter (event) monitor; - Lab: - Hemoglobin A1c - Lipid panel - Complete Blood Count - EMS/ambulance run sheet (if applicable); - Emergency Department records (if applicable); and - If age 40 or older at time of event, a carotid duplex ultrasound performed within the previous one (1) year.",DEFER Submit the information to the FAA for a possible Special Issuance.,"<p><strong>B.</strong> Unknown or unexplained cause</p>
<p>OR</p>
<p>Multiple unrelated syncopal events</p>
<p>If due to a cardiac cause such as myocardial infarction or ischemia, see that page</p>","<p>Submit the following for FAA review:</p>
<p>Testing must be <strong>performed within the past 90 days</strong> to be considered current.</p>
<ul><li><a href=""https://www.faa.gov/ame_guide/media/Cardiovascular_Evaluation_Protocol.pdf"" target=""_blank"" rel=""noopener"">• Cardiac Evaluation</a> <strong>; </strong></li><li>Echocardiogram (Echo);</li><li>Exercise Stress Test (EST);</li><li>14-day Holter (event) monitor;</li><li>Lab:<ul><li>Hemoglobin A1c</li><li>Lipid panel</li><li>Complete Blood Count</li></ul></li><li>EMS/ambulance run sheet (if applicable);</li><li>Emergency Department records (if applicable); and</li><li>If age 40 or older at time of event, a carotid duplex ultrasound performed within the previous one (1) year.</li></ul>","<p><strong>DEFER </strong></p>
<p>Submit the information to the FAA for a possible Special Issuance.</p>"
coronary-heart-disease,CORONARY HEART DISEASE,C. Unexplained syncope AFTER a cardiac evaluation has been performed (and no cardiac cause found),"Submit the following for FAA review: - Items in Row B - A current, detailed neurological evaluation that meets FAA Specifications for Neurologic Evaluation generated from a clinic visit with the treating neurologist no more than 90 days before the AME exam. Note: If no definitive cause for syncope (e.g., unexplained loss of consciousness), a two (2) year recovery period is required. If head injury occurred, see that page.",DEFER Submit the information to the FAA.,<p>C. Unexplained syncope AFTER a cardiac evaluation has been performed (and no cardiac cause found)</p>,"<p>Submit the following for FAA review:</p>
<ul><li>Items in Row B</li><li>A current, detailed neurological evaluation that meets <a href=""https://www.faa.gov/sites/faa.gov/files/NeurologicalSpecificationSheet.pdf"" target=""_blank"" rel=""noopener"">FAA Specifications for Neurologic Evaluation</a> generated from a clinic visit with the treating neurologist no more than 90 days before the AME exam.</li></ul>
<p><strong>Note:</strong> If no definitive cause for syncope (e.g., unexplained loss of consciousness), a <strong>two (2) year recovery period is required</strong>.</p>
<p>If head injury occurred, see that page.</p>","<p>DEFER</p>
<p>Submit the information to the FAA.</p>"
