endocarditis,ENDOCARDITIS,"A. Current or historical diagnosis If resulting in cardiac valve repair or valve replacement, see that page.","Submit the following for FAA review: 1. A current, detailed Clinical Progress Note generated from a clinic visit with an infectious disease specialist or cardiologist no more than 90 days before the AME exam. It should include a summary of the history of the condition or diagnosis; current medications, dosages, and side effects (if any); clinical exam findings; results of any testing performed; diagnosis; assessment and plan (prognosis); and follow-up. 2. Echocardiogram (Echo). Copies of a 2- D and Doppler flow study report performed no more than 90 days prior to the AME exam. 3. Other testing: Any deemed clinically necessary and already performed by the treating physician. 4. Hospital records: History and Physical (H&P), operative notes, and discharge summary (if applicable).",DEFER Submit the information to the FAA for a possible Special Issuance Annotate (elements or findings) in Block 60.,"<p><strong>A. Current or historical diagnosis </strong>If resulting in cardiac valve repair or valve replacement, see that page.</p>","<p>Submit the following for FAA review:</p>
<p><strong>1. </strong>A current, detailed Clinical Progress Note generated from a clinic visit with <strong>an infectious disease specialist or cardiologist </strong>no more than 90 days before the AME exam.</p>
<p>It should include a summary of the history of the condition or diagnosis; current medications, dosages, and side effects (if any); clinical exam findings; results of any testing performed; diagnosis; assessment and plan (prognosis); and follow-up.</p>
<p><strong>2. Echocardiogram (Echo)</strong>. Copies of a 2- D and Doppler flow study report performed no more than <strong>90 days prior </strong>to the AME exam.</p>
<p><strong>3. </strong>Other testing: Any deemed clinically necessary and already performed by the treating physician.</p>
<p><strong>4. </strong>Hospital records: History and Physical (H&amp;P), operative notes, and discharge summary (if applicable).</p>","<p><strong>DEFER</strong></p>
<p>Submit the information to the FAA for a possible Special Issuance</p>
<p>Annotate (elements or findings) in Block 60.</p>"
endocarditis,ENDOCARDITIS,A. MILD or TRACE (based on ECHO results) - Mitral Valve regurgitation; or - Mitral Valve insufficiency; or - Mitral Valve Prolapse (MVP); AND Asymptomatic,The AME should review: - 1. Echocardiogram (Echo). Copies of the most recent 2-D and Doppler flow study report. OR A clinical problem list or progress note which lists the echo findings as mild. If the AME can determine the condition is Asymptomatic and the valve disease is MILD:,ISSUE Annotate this information in Block 60.,"<p><strong>A. </strong></p>
<p><strong>MILD or TRACE</strong></p>
<p>(based on ECHO results)</p>
<ul><li>Mitral Valve regurgitation;</li></ul>
<p>or</p>
<ul><li>Mitral Valve insufficiency;</li></ul>
<p>or</p>
<ul><li>Mitral Valve Prolapse (MVP);</li></ul>
<p>AND</p>
<p><strong>Asymptomatic </strong></p>","<p>The AME should review:</p>
<ul><li>1. <strong>Echocardiogram (Echo)</strong>. Copies of the <strong>most recent</strong> 2-D and Doppler flow study report.</li></ul>
<p>OR</p>
<p>A clinical problem list or progress note which lists the echo findings as mild.</p>
<p>If the AME can determine the condition is Asymptomatic and the valve disease is MILD:</p>","<p><strong>ISSUE</strong></p>
<p>Annotate this</p>
<p>information in</p>
<p>Block 60.</p>"
