congenital-heart-conditions,CONGENITAL HEART CONDITIONS,C. • Atrioventricular Septal Defect (ASD) • Coarctation of the Aorta* • Double-outlet Right Ventricle • d-Transposition of the Great Arteries • Ebstein Anomaly • Hypoplastic Left Heart Syndrome • Interrupted Aortic Arch •Patent Ductus Arteriosus (PDA) • Pulmonary Atresia • Single Ventricle • Tetralogy of Fallot • Total Anomalous Pulmonary Venous Return • Tricuspid Atresia • Truncus Arteriosus • Ventricular Septal Defect (VSD) OR Any other congenital heart/cardiac condition,"Submit the following for FAA review: - 1. A current, detailed Clinical Progress Note generated from a clinic visit with their treating cardiologist no more than 90 days before the AME exam. It should include a summary of the history of the condition or diagnosis; current medications, dosages, and side effects (if any); clinical exam findings; results of any testing performed; diagnosis; assessment and plan (prognosis); and follow-up. If surgery was remote, and they are no longer seeing their cardiologist, the progress note can be from a board-certified cardiologist. - 2. Echocardiogram (Echo). Report and images from a 2-D and Doppler flow study performed no more than 90 days prior to the AME exam. - 3. 24-hour cardiac monitor performed no more than 90 days prior to the AME exam. ≥ 24-hour cardiac monitor (such as a Holter, Zio Patch, etc.). It should have atrial and ventricular ectopic counts; hourly tabular data to include the longest pause duration and counts of all pauses > 2.0 or 2.5 seconds; heart rate (max, min, and average); other histograms and frequency graphs; and percentage of atrial fibrillation/flutter. - 4. Exercise stress test (EST) performed no more than 90 days prior to the AME exam. - 5. Operative report(s) from all cardiac/heart surgery performed. (if applicable) - 6. Copies of any advanced imaging [e.g., Chest Computed Tomography (CT) or Magnetic Resonance Imaging (MRI)] already performed. Include both Report AND actual images. 7. * Coarctation of the Aorta, must also include a Brain MRA performed no more than 90 days prior to the AME exam. Note: Once these records are reviewed, additional testing or information may be required.",DEFER Submit the information to the FAA for a possible Special Issuance. Summarize findings in Item 60.,"<p><strong>C. </strong></p>
<p>• Atrioventricular Septal Defect (ASD)</p>
<p>• Coarctation of the Aorta*</p>
<p>• Double-outlet Right Ventricle</p>
<p>• d-Transposition of the Great Arteries</p>
<p>• Ebstein Anomaly</p>
<p>• Hypoplastic Left Heart Syndrome</p>
<p>• Interrupted Aortic Arch</p>
<p>•Patent Ductus Arteriosus (PDA)</p>
<p>• Pulmonary Atresia</p>
<p>• Single Ventricle</p>
<p>• Tetralogy of Fallot</p>
<p>• Total Anomalous Pulmonary Venous Return</p>
<p>• Tricuspid Atresia</p>
<p>• Truncus Arteriosus</p>
<p>• Ventricular Septal Defect (VSD)</p>
<p>OR</p>
<p>Any other congenital heart/cardiac condition</p>","<p>Submit the following for FAA review:</p>
<ul><li><strong>1. </strong>A <a href=""https://www.faa.gov/ame_guide/media/PilotInformation_DetailedClinicalProgressNote.pdf"" target=""_blank"" rel=""noopener"">current, detailed Clinical Progress Note</a> generated from a clinic visit with their treating <strong>cardiologist</strong> no more than 90 days before the AME exam.</li></ul>
<p>It should include a summary of the history of the condition or diagnosis; current medications, dosages, and side effects (if any); clinical exam findings; results of any testing performed; diagnosis; assessment and plan (prognosis); and follow-up.</p>
<p>If surgery was remote, and they are no longer seeing their cardiologist, the progress note can be from a board-certified cardiologist.</p>
<ul><li><strong>2. Echocardiogram (Echo). Report and images </strong>from a 2-D and Doppler flow study performed no more than 90 days prior to the AME exam.</li></ul>
<ul><li><strong>3. 24-hour cardiac monitor</strong> performed no more than 90 days prior to the AME exam.</li></ul>
<p>≥ 24-hour cardiac monitor (such as a Holter, Zio Patch, etc.). It should have atrial and ventricular ectopic counts; hourly tabular data to include the longest pause duration and counts of all pauses &gt; 2.0 or 2.5 seconds; heart rate (max, min, and average); other histograms and frequency graphs; and percentage of atrial fibrillation/flutter.</p>
<ul><li><strong>4. Exercise stress test (EST)</strong> performed no more than 90 days prior to the AME exam.</li></ul>
<ul><li><strong>5. Operative report(s)</strong> from <strong>all </strong>cardiac/heart surgery performed. (if applicable)</li></ul>
<ul><li><strong>6. </strong>Copies of any advanced imaging [e.g., Chest Computed Tomography (CT) or Magnetic Resonance Imaging (MRI)] already performed. Include both Report AND actual images.</li></ul>
<p><strong>7. </strong>* <strong>Coarctation of the Aorta, </strong>must also include a <strong>Brain MRA</strong> performed no more than 90 days prior to the AME exam.</p>
<p>Note: Once these records are reviewed, additional testing or information may be required.</p>","<p><strong>DEFER </strong></p>
<p>Submit the information to the FAA for a possible Special Issuance.</p>
<p>Summarize findings in Item 60.</p>"
fibromuscular-dysplasia,FIBROMUSCULAR DYSPLASIA,A. Any history,"Submit the following for FAA review: - 1. A current, detailed Clinical Progress Note generated from a clinic visit from the physician (who made the diagnosis or follows clinically) no more than 90 days before the AME exam. It should include a summary of the history of the condition or diagnosis; current medications, dosages, and side effects (if any); clinical exam findings; results of any testing performed; diagnosis; assessment and plan (prognosis); and follow-up. - 2. Imaging (MRA or CTA) of major vascular systems performed within the previous two (2) years. Submit reports for images of: - Brain; - Head and neck; - Coronary arteries (CTA); and - Abdomen and pelvis to include iliac arteries. - 3. Other testing: Copies of any other testing already performed by the treating physician.",DEFER Submit the information to the FAA for a possible Special Issuance. Annotate (elements or findings) in Block 60.,"<p><strong>A. </strong></p>
