buerger-disease-or-thromboangiitis-obliterans-tao,Buerger Disease or Thromboangiitis Obliterans (TAO),B. Current or Historical Diagnosis WITH complications OR continued SMOKING,"Submit the following for FAA review: - 1. A current, detailed Clinical Progress Note generated from a clinic visit with their cardiologist or treating physician no more than 90 days before the AME exam. It should include a summary of the history of the condition or diagnosis; current medications, dosages, and side effects (if any); clinical exam findings; results of any testing performed; diagnosis; assessment and plan (prognosis); and follow-up. - 2. Personal Statement (typed) describing your history of tobacco use in any form (e.g. cigarettes, cigars, pipes, vapes, or chewing tobacco) or tobacco cessation aids (e.g., vapes, gum, patches, lozenges, Chantix). - Include start and stop dates (MM/YYYY), daily amount used, and whether you currently use tobacco. - If currently using any form of tobacco, list the type, how much, and how often. - 3. Results of any other testing already performed by the treating physician.",DEFER Submit the information to the FAA for a possible Special Issuance. Summarize findings in Item 60.,<p><strong>B. </strong> Current or Historical Diagnosis WITH complications OR continued SMOKING</p>,"<p><strong>Submit the following for FAA review: </strong></p>
<ul><li><strong>1. </strong>A <a href=""https://www.faa.gov/ame_guide/media/PilotInformation_DetailedClinicalProgressNote.pdf"" target=""_blank"" rel=""noopener"">current, detailed Clinical Progress Note</a> generated from a clinic visit with their <strong>cardiologist</strong> or treating physician no more than 90 days before the AME exam.</li></ul>
<p>It should include a summary of the history of the condition or diagnosis; current medications, dosages, and side effects (if any); clinical exam findings; results of any testing performed; diagnosis; assessment and plan (prognosis); and follow-up.</p>
<ul><li><strong>2. </strong>Personal Statement (typed) describing your <strong>history of tobacco use</strong> in any form (e.g. cigarettes, cigars, pipes, vapes, or chewing tobacco) <strong>or tobacco cessation aids</strong> (e.g., vapes, gum, patches, lozenges, Chantix).</li><li>Include start and stop dates (MM/YYYY), daily amount used, and whether you currently use tobacco.</li><li>If currently using any form of tobacco, list the type, how much, and how often.</li></ul>
<ul><li><strong>3. </strong>Results of any other testing already performed by the treating physician.</li></ul>","<p><strong>DEFER </strong></p>
