<p>Summarize findings in Item 60.</p>"
postural-tachycardia-syndrome-pots,POSTURAL TACHYCARDIA SYNDROME (POTS),"A. Any history Note: In most cases, a diagnosis of POTS is not acceptable for medical certification/clearance.","Submit the following for FAA review: - 12. A current, detailed Clinical Progress Note generated from a clinic visit with the treating cardiologist or neurologist performed no more than 90 days before the AME exam. It should include a summary of the history of the condition or diagnosis; current medications, dosages, and side effects (if any); clinical exam findings; results of any testing performed; diagnosis; assessment and plan (prognosis); and follow-up. - 13. It must specifically include if the diagnosis of POTS is: - Confirmed; - Equivocal; or - Not confirmed - 14. Copies of any other treatment records or testing already performed by any providers for this or any similar condition by the treating physician. - Doctor's office notes; - Consultant notes; - Results from any testing already performed for the condition; and - Hospital records: History and Physical (H&P), operative notes, and discharge summary (if applicable). Note: To rescind the diagnosis of POTS, submit an evaluation performed by: • POTS center of excellence; • A neurologist specializing in autonomic nervous system disorders; OR • A researcher with extensive experience in POTS.",DEFER Submit the information to the FAA.,"<p><strong>A. </strong></p>
<p>Any history</p>
<p><strong>Note:</strong> In most cases, a diagnosis of POTS is not acceptable for medical certification/clearance.</p>","<p><strong>Submit the following for FAA review: </strong></p>
<ul><li><strong>12. </strong>A <a href=""https://www.faa.gov/ame_guide/media/PilotInformation_DetailedClinicalProgressNote.pdf"" target=""_blank"" rel=""noopener"">current, detailed Clinical Progress Note</a> generated from a clinic visit with the treating <strong>cardiologist or neurologist</strong> performed no more than 90 days before the AME exam.</li></ul>
<p>It should include a summary of the history of the condition or diagnosis; current medications, dosages, and side effects (if any); clinical exam findings; results of any testing performed; diagnosis; assessment and plan (prognosis); and follow-up.</p>
<ul><li><strong>13. </strong>It <strong>must specifically include</strong> if the diagnosis of POTS is:<ul><li>Confirmed;</li><li>Equivocal; or</li><li>Not confirmed</li></ul></li></ul>
<ul><li><strong>14. </strong>Copies of any other treatment records or testing already performed by any providers for this or any similar condition by the treating physician.</li></ul>
<ul><li>Doctor&#x27;s office notes;</li><li>Consultant notes;</li><li>Results from any testing already performed for the condition; and</li><li>Hospital records: History and Physical (H&amp;P), operative notes, and discharge summary (if applicable).</li></ul>
<p><strong>Note: </strong>To rescind the diagnosis of POTS, submit an evaluation performed by:</p>
<p>• POTS center of excellence;</p>
<p>• A neurologist specializing in autonomic nervous system disorders; OR</p>
<p>• A researcher with extensive experience in POTS.</p>","<p><strong>DEFER </strong></p>
<p>Submit the information to the FAA.</p>"
