<p>Block 60 <strong>and submit</strong> the evaluation to the FAA for retention in the file.</p>"
item-38-abdomen-and-viscera,ITEM 38. Abdomen and Viscera,B. Non-alcoholic cirrhosis,"Submit the following for FAA review: - 1. A current, detailed Clinical Progress Note generated from a clinic visit with the treating hepatologist (liver specialist) or gastroenterologist no more than 90 days before the AME exam. It must include a detailed summary of the history of the condition; current medications, dosage, and side effects (if any); physical exam findings; results of any testing performed; diagnosis; assessment; plan (prognosis); and follow-up. - 2. It must specifically include: - How the condition was diagnosed, etiology, hospitalizations, - If there is ANY history of hepatic encephalopathy, ascites or varices. - Calculation of Child-Pugh score - 3. Lab: Performed within 90 days of exam to include: - CBC; - Comprehensive metabolic panel; - GGT; - Alpha-fetoprotein; and - PT/PTT/INR","DEFER Submit the information to the FAA for a possible Special Issuance Annotate (elements or findings) in Item 60. - 4. Most recent imaging studies (e.g., ultrasound, MRI, etc.) - 5. Most recent upper endoscopy report and any associated pathology reports - 6. Biopsy results (if performed) - 7. Neuropsychological Evaluation with interpretation of CogScreen-Aeromedical Edition.* - 8. Results of any other testing deemed appropriate by the treating physician. *Note: If CogScreen-AE is interpreted as abnormal, completion of neurocognitive testing per specs for Potential Neurocognitive Impairment is indicated.","<p><strong>B. </strong></p>
<p>Non-alcoholic cirrhosis</p>","<p>Submit the following for FAA review:</p>
<ul><li><strong>1. </strong>A <strong>current, detailed Clinical Progress Note</strong> generated from a clinic visit with the treating <strong>hepatologist (liver specialist) or gastroenterologist</strong> no more than <strong>90 days before</strong> the AME exam. It must include a detailed summary of the history of the condition; current medications, dosage, and side effects (if any); physical exam findings; results of any testing performed; diagnosis; assessment; plan (prognosis); and follow-up.</li><li><strong>2. </strong>It must specifically include:<ul><li>How the condition was diagnosed, etiology, hospitalizations,</li><li>If there is ANY history of hepatic encephalopathy, ascites or varices.</li><li>Calculation of <strong>Child-Pugh score</strong></li></ul></li><li><strong>3. Lab: </strong>Performed within 90 days of exam to include:<ul><li>CBC;</li><li>Comprehensive metabolic panel;</li><li>GGT;</li><li>Alpha-fetoprotein; and</li><li>PT/PTT/INR</li></ul></li></ul>","<p><strong>DEFER </strong></p>
<p>Submit the information to the FAA for a possible Special Issuance</p>
<p>Annotate (elements or findings) in</p>
<p>Item 60.</p>
<ul><li><strong>4. </strong>Most recent imaging studies (e.g., ultrasound, MRI, etc.)</li><li><strong>5. </strong>Most recent upper endoscopy report and any associated pathology reports</li><li><strong>6. </strong>Biopsy results (if performed)</li><li><strong>7. </strong>Neuropsychological Evaluation with interpretation of CogScreen-Aeromedical Edition.*</li><li><strong>8. </strong>Results of any other testing deemed appropriate by the treating physician.</li></ul>
<p>*Note: If CogScreen-AE is interpreted as abnormal, completion of neurocognitive testing per specs for Potential Neurocognitive Impairment is indicated.</p>"
