eosinophilic-esophagitis,Eosinophilic Esophagitis,B. Recipient,"After a six (6) month post-transplant recovery period with documented stability for the last three (3) months: Submit the following for FAA review: - 1. A current, detailed Clinical Progress Note generated from a clinic visit with the transplant surgeon or transplant team physician no more than 90 days before the AME exam from transplant surgeon or transplant team physician. It should include a detailed summary of the history of the condition or diagnosis; treatments and outcomes; current medications, dosages, and side effects (if any); physical exam findings; all pertinent test results obtained; assessment; plan (prognosis); and follow-up. - 2. It must specifically include: Indication for transplant, any sequelae prior to transplant, if alcohol was a contributing factor (abuse or dependence), status of the transplant, functional capacity, modifiable risk factors, and prognosis for incapacitation. - 3. Any recent or expected change in treatment plan. - 4. Complication history such as: - Rejection or graft versus host disease/GVHD; - Infection Hepatitis C (HCV) or CMV; and/or","DEFER Submit the information to the FAA for a possible Special Issuance Annotate (elements or findings) in Item 60. - - Malignancy due to hepatocellular carcinoma (HCC) or following transplant and initiation of immune-suppressants. - 5. Lab: Complete blood count (CBC), CMP with LFTs performed within the past 90 days. - 6. Imaging: Copies of the initial and most recent MRI, CT, or PET scan with clinical interpretation. - 7. Specific testing: Results of liver biopsy (already performed). - 8. Hospital records: History and Physical (H&P), operative notes, and discharge summary. - 9. Pre-transplant treatment notes that identify the diagnosis/underlying condition which required transplant.",<p><strong>B. </strong>Recipient</p>,"<p>After a <strong>six (6) month post-transplant</strong> recovery period with <strong>documented stability for the last three (3) months:</strong></p>
<p>Submit the following for FAA review:</p>
