arteriovenous-malformation-avm-neurological-brain-or-spinal-cord,ARTERIOVENOUS MALFORMATION (AVM) – Neurological (Brain or Spinal Cord),A. Simple Febrile Seizure occurring at Age 5 or younger (fever seizure/febrile seizure),"If the AME can determine all of the following apply: - A single seizure only; - Condition fully resolved age 5 or younger; - NO recurrence; - NO anticonvulsant medication given; AND - Condition has resolved without sequelae with NO symptoms or current problems that would interfere with flight duties: If the AME is unable to determine all of the above information, a detailed neurological evaluation that meets FAA Specifications for Neurologic Evaluation generated from a clinic visit with the treating neurologist will be required. If the neurology evaluation verifies the condition was a simple febrile seizure:","ISSUE Annotate this information in Block 60. All others, go to Row C",<p><strong>A.</strong> Simple Febrile Seizure occurring at <strong>Age 5 or younger</strong> (fever seizure/febrile seizure)</p>,"<p>If the AME can determine all of the following apply:</p>
<ul><li>A <strong>single seizure only</strong>;</li><li>Condition fully resolved age 5 or younger;</li><li>NO recurrence;</li><li>NO anticonvulsant medication given; AND</li><li>Condition has resolved without sequelae with NO symptoms or current problems that would interfere with flight duties:</li></ul>
<p>If the AME is unable to determine all of the above information, a <strong>detailed neurological evaluation</strong> that meets <a href=""https://www.faa.gov/ame_guide/media/NeurologicalSpecificationSheet.pdf"" target=""_blank"" rel=""noopener"">FAA Specifications for Neurologic Evaluation</a> generated from a clinic visit with the treating neurologist will be required.</p>
<p>If the neurology evaluation verifies the condition was a simple febrile seizure:</p>","<p><strong>ISSUE</strong></p>
<p>Annotate this</p>
<p>information in</p>
<p>Block 60.</p>
<p>All others,</p>
<p>go to Row C</p>"
arteriovenous-malformation-avm-neurological-brain-or-spinal-cord,ARTERIOVENOUS MALFORMATION (AVM) – Neurological (Brain or Spinal Cord),B. Single seizure even provoked by a known cause which has been corrected May be due to: Electrolyte or severe metabolic imbalance; Medication use; or Convulsive syncope; If due to TBI or post concussive seizure - see that section If due to drug or alcohol withdrawal - see D&A section,"After a One (1)-year recovery period, submit the following for FAA review: - 1. A current, detailed neurological evaluation that meets FAA Specifications for Neurologic Evaluation generated from a clinic visit with the treating neurologist no more than 90 days before the AME exam. - 2. It must specifically include the date of last seizure activity and dates medication discontinued. - 3. *MRI brain performed at any time after the seizure activity started. - - If not already performed, a current brain MRI is required. - - Submit BOTH the interpretive report on paper and imaging on CD in DICOM readable format (there must be a file named 'DICOMDIR' in the root directory - - of the CD-ROM). Please verify the CD will display the images before sending. Retain a copy of all films as a safeguard if lost in the mail. - 4. Electroencephalogram (EEG) performed no more than 12 months before the AME exam. It must be sleep-deprived EEG: Awake, asleep, and with provocation (hyperventilation, photic/strobe light). - If not already performed, a current EEG is required. - Submit any previous EEG(s) available for comparison. - Submit BOTH the interpretive report on paper and imaging on CD in DICOM readable format (there must be a file named 'DICOMDIR' in the root directory of the CD-ROM). Please verify the CD will display the images before sending. Retain a copy of all films as a safeguard if lost in the mail. - 5. FAA Airman Seizure Questionnaire completed by the applicant. Note: In some cases, a longer recovery period will be required based on the underlying cause.",DEFER Submit the information to the FAA for a possible Special Issuance,"<p><strong>B. Single seizure </strong>even <strong>provoked </strong>by a known cause which has been corrected</p>
<p>May be due to:</p>
<p>Electrolyte or severe metabolic imbalance;</p>
<p>Medication use;</p>
<p>or</p>
<p>Convulsive syncope;</p>
<p>If due to TBI or post concussive seizure - see that section</p>
<p>If due to drug or alcohol withdrawal - see D&amp;A section</p>","<p>After a <strong>One (1)-year recovery </strong>period, submit the following for FAA review:</p>
<ul><li>1. A <strong>current, </strong>d<strong>etailed neurological evaluation</strong> that meets <a href=""https://www.faa.gov/ame_guide/media/NeurologicalSpecificationSheet.pdf"" target=""_blank"" rel=""noopener"">FAA Specifications for Neurologic Evaluation</a> generated from a clinic visit with the <strong>treating neurologist no more than 90 days</strong> before the AME exam.</li></ul>
<ul><li>2. It <strong>must specifically include</strong> the date of last seizure activity and dates medication discontinued.</li></ul>
<ul><li>3. <strong>*MRI brain</strong> performed at any time after the seizure activity started.</li></ul>
<ul><li><ul><li>If not already performed, a current brain MRI is required.</li></ul></li></ul>
<ul><li><ul><li>Submit BOTH the interpretive report on paper and imaging on CD in DICOM readable format (there must be a file named &#x27;DICOMDIR&#x27; in the root directory</li></ul></li></ul>
<ul><li><ul><li>of the CD-ROM). Please verify the CD will display the images before sending. Retain a copy of all films as a safeguard if lost in the mail.</li></ul></li></ul>
<ul><li><p>4. <strong>Electroencephalogram (EEG) </strong>performed <strong>no more than 12 months before the AME exam</strong>. It must be sleep-deprived EEG: Awake, asleep, and with provocation (hyperventilation, photic/strobe light).</p>
<ul><li>If not already performed, a current EEG is required.</li><li>Submit any previous EEG(s) available for comparison.</li><li>Submit BOTH the interpretive report on paper and imaging on CD in DICOM readable format (there must be a file named &#x27;DICOMDIR&#x27; in the root directory of the CD-ROM). Please verify the CD will display the images before sending. Retain a copy of all films as a safeguard if lost in the mail.</li></ul></li></ul>
<ul><li><a href=""https://www.faa.gov/ame_guide/media/Airman_Seizure_Questionnaire.pdf"" target=""_blank"" rel=""noopener"">5. FAA Airman Seizure Questionnaire</a> completed by the applicant.</li></ul>
<p><strong>Note:</strong> In some cases, a longer recovery period will be required based on the underlying cause.</p>","<p><strong>DEFER</strong></p>
<p>Submit the information to the FAA for a possible Special Issuance</p>"
arteriovenous-malformation-avm-neurological-brain-or-spinal-cord,ARTERIOVENOUS MALFORMATION (AVM) – Neurological (Brain or Spinal Cord),"C. Single seizure event UNPROVOKED (No known cause) OR Complex febrile seizure; Atypical/complex febrile seizures; or febrile seizures treated with medication as a child (usually age 5 or younger). Note: If 2 or more seizures in a lifetime, from any cause, go to the Epilepsy section.","After a four (4)-year recovery period and the last two (2) years must be without anticonvulsant medication, submit the following for FAA review: - All information in Row B. Upon review, additional information may be required.",DEFER Submit the information to the FAA for a possible Special Issuance,"<p><strong>C. Single </strong>seizure event <strong>UNPROVOKED</strong></p>
