prediabetes,PREDIABETES,"C. Treated with TWO (2) or more diabetic medication (non-insulin) components Note: If the medication is taken for weight loss, and the individual has a diagnosis of diabetes, see www.faa.gov/go/diabetic","Submit either: 1. Diabetes or Hyperglycemia on Oral Medications Status Report (The treating physician must clearly indicate the reason for the medication and if there is any history of diabetes.) OR 2. A current, detailed Clinical Progress Note from the treating physician which contains all the required information listed in the above status report. - It must include the indication for the medication and if there is any history of diabetes or not; - Hemoglobin A1c lab performed no more than 90 days before the AME exam.",DEFER Submit the information to the FAA for a possible Special Issuance Annotate (elements or findings) in Block 60.,"<p><strong>C. </strong></p>
<p>Treated with</p>
<p>TWO (2) or more</p>
<p>diabetic medication</p>
<p><strong>(non-insulin) </strong>components</p>
<p><strong>Note:</strong> If the medication is taken for weight loss, and the individual has a diagnosis of diabetes, see <a href=""http://www.faa.gov/go/diabetic"" target=""_blank"" rel=""noopener"">www.faa.gov/go/diabetic</a></p>","<p>Submit either:</p>
<p>1. <a href=""https://www.faa.gov/ame_guide/media/diabetes_or_hyperglycemia_on_oral_meds_report.pdf"" target=""_blank"" rel=""noopener"">Diabetes or Hyperglycemia on Oral Medications Status Report</a></p>
<p>(The treating physician must clearly <strong>indicate the reason for the medication and if there is any history of diabetes.)</strong></p>
<p><strong> OR </strong></p>
<p>2. A <strong>current, detailed Clinical Progress Note</strong> from the treating physician which contains all the required information listed in the above status report.</p>
<ul><li>It must include the <strong>indication for the medication and if there is any history of diabetes or not</strong>;</li></ul>
<ul><li>Hemoglobin A1c lab performed<strong> no more than 90 days before</strong> the AME exam.</li></ul>","<p><strong>DEFER </strong></p>
