diabetes-insipidus-or-polyuria,DIABETES INSIPIDUS OR POLYURIA,"Primary polydipsia (dipsogenic or psychogenic) If due to a neurologic condition such as a tumor, infection, stroke, neurosurgery, or head injury, see that condition page.","1. A current, detailed Clinical Progress Note generated from a clinic visit with a board-certified endocrinologist, nephrologist or treating physician no more than 90 days prior to the AME exam. It must include: - A detailed summary of the history of the condition; including etiology; - Current medications, dosage, and side effects (if any); - Physical exam findings; - Results of any testing performed; - Diagnosis; - Assessment and plan; - Prognosis; and - Follow-up. 2. Copies of any lab performed for evaluation of this condition. 3. Copies of any imaging (CT/MRI, etc.) already performed. Note: Psychiatric evaluation will be requested if the documents show the condition is psychogenic polydipsia.",DEFER Submit the information to the FAA for a possible Special Issuance Annotate (elements or findings) in Block 60.,"<p><strong> Primary polydipsia</strong></p>
<p>(dipsogenic or psychogenic)</p>
<p>If due to a neurologic</p>
<p>condition such as a tumor, infection, stroke, neurosurgery, or head injury, see that condition page.</p>","<p><strong>1.</strong> A <strong>current, detailed Clinical Progress Note</strong> generated from a clinic visit with a board-certified endocrinologist, nephrologist or treating physician no more than <strong>90 days prior </strong>to the AME exam. It must include:</p>
<ul><li>A detailed summary of the history of the condition; including etiology;</li><li>Current medications, dosage, and side effects (if any);</li><li>Physical exam findings;</li><li>Results of any testing performed;</li><li>Diagnosis;</li><li>Assessment and plan;</li><li>Prognosis; and</li><li>Follow-up.</li></ul>
<p><strong>2.</strong> Copies of any lab performed for evaluation of this condition.</p>
<p><strong>3.</strong> Copies of any imaging (CT/MRI, etc.) already performed.</p>
<p><strong>Note:</strong> Psychiatric evaluation will be requested if the documents show the condition is psychogenic polydipsia.</p>","<p><strong>DEFER </strong></p>
<p>Submit the information to the FAA for a possible Special Issuance</p>
<p>Annotate (elements or findings) in Block 60.</p>"
acromegaly,ACROMEGALY,A. Due to pituitary tumor NOTE: Must submit this information AND Any required pituitary tumor information.,"Submit the following for FAA review: - 1. Sleep Study that meets current AASM or CMS Guidelines for a Type I or Type II sleep study (Type III or Type IV NOT allowed) performed no more than 12 months before the AME exam. (If currently treated for OSA, see that page.) - 2. A current, detailed Clinical Progress Note generated from a clinic visit with a cardiologist no more than 90 days before the AME exam. It should include a summary of the history of the condition or diagnosis; current medications, dosages, and side effects (if any); clinical exam findings; results of any testing performed; diagnosis; assessment and plan (prognosis); and follow-up. - 3. Labs to include lipids and hemoglobin A1c performed no more than 90 days before the AME exam. - 4. Echocardiogram (Echo). Copies of a 2- D and Doppler flow study report performed no more than 90 days prior to the AME exam. - 5. 24-hour cardiac monitor performed no more than 90 days prior to the AME exam. ≥ 24-hour cardiac monitor (such as a Holter, Zio Patch, etc.). It should have atrial and ventricular ectopic counts; hourly tabular data to include the longest pause duration and counts of all pauses > 2.0 or 2.5 seconds; heart rate (max, min, and average); other histograms and frequency graphs; and percentage of atrial fibrillation/flutter. - 6. A Neuropsychological evaluation that meets **FAA Specifications for Neuropsychological Evaluations for Potential Neurocognitive Impairment** from a clinic visit with the treating neuropsychologist no more than 90 days before the AME exam. - 7. Other records and testing: Copies of prior records and any testing already performed by the treating physician. - 8. All items listed on the correct row of the PITUITARY ADENOMA page.",DEFER Submit the information to the FAA for a possible Special Issuance,"<p><strong>A. Due to pituitary tumor </strong></p>
<p><strong>NOTE: </strong></p>
<p>Must submit this information</p>
<p>AND</p>
<p>Any required pituitary tumor information.</p>","<p><strong>Submit the following for FAA review: </strong></p>
<ul><li><strong>1. Sleep Study</strong> that meets current AASM or CMS Guidelines for a Type I or Type II sleep study (Type III or Type IV NOT allowed) performed no more than 12 months before the AME exam. (If currently treated for OSA, see that page.)</li></ul>
<ul><li><strong>2. </strong>A <a href=""https://www.faa.gov/ame_guide/media/PilotInformation_DetailedClinicalProgressNote.pdf"" target=""_blank"" rel=""noopener"">current, detailed Clinical Progress Note</a> generated from a clinic visit with a <strong>cardiologist</strong> no more than 90 days before the AME exam.</li></ul>
<p>It should include a summary of the history of the condition or diagnosis; current medications, dosages, and side effects (if any); clinical exam findings; results of any testing performed; diagnosis; assessment and plan (prognosis); and follow-up.</p>
<ul><li><strong>3. </strong>Labs to include <strong>lipids and hemoglobin A1c</strong> performed no more than 90 days before the AME exam.</li></ul>
<ul><li><strong>4. Echocardiogram (Echo)</strong>. Copies of a 2- D and Doppler flow study report performed no more than 90 days prior to the AME exam.</li></ul>
<ul><li><strong>5. 24-hour cardiac monitor</strong> performed no more than 90 days prior to the AME exam.</li></ul>
<p>≥ 24-hour cardiac monitor (such as a Holter, Zio Patch, etc.). It should have atrial and ventricular ectopic counts; hourly tabular data to include the longest pause duration and counts of all pauses &gt; 2.0 or 2.5 seconds; heart rate (max, min, and average); other histograms and frequency graphs; and percentage of atrial fibrillation/flutter.</p>
<ul><li><strong>6. </strong>A Neuropsychological evaluation that meets **FAA Specifications for Neuropsychological Evaluations for Potential Neurocognitive Impairment** from a clinic visit with the treating neuropsychologist no more than 90 days before the AME exam.</li></ul>
<ul><li><strong>7. </strong>Other records and testing: Copies of prior records and any testing already performed by the treating physician.</li><li><strong>8. </strong>All items listed on the correct row of the <a href=""https://www.faa.gov/ame_guide/media/Dispo_Table_Pituitary_Adenoma.pdf"" target=""_blank"" rel=""noopener"">PITUITARY ADENOMA</a> page.</li></ul>","<p><strong> DEFER </strong></p>
