cushing-syndrome,CUSHING SYNDROME,"A. Any history If due to pituitary adenoma or other cause, see that page.","Submit the following for FAA review: - 1. A current, detailed Clinical Progress Note generated from a clinic visit with the treating Endocrinologist no more than 90 days before the AME exam. It must include a detailed summary of the history of the condition; current medications, dosages, and side effects (if any); physical exam findings; results of any testing performed; diagnosis; assessment; plan (prognosis); and follow-up. It must specifically include: - Cardiovascular risk factors; - Functional capacity; - Any concern for OSA; and - Any neuropsychological or psychiatric concerns. - 2. Labs. Hemoglobin A1c no more than 90 days prior to exam. Any other labs already performed or clinically indicated. - 3. Operative and pathology report(s), if applicable. - 4. Reports of imaging studies (CT/MRI/ultrasound) already performed. After reviewing the above, some cases will require a Neuropsychological Evaluation in accordance with the Potential Neurocognitive Impairment specification sheet.",DEFER Submit the information to the FAA for a possible Special Issuance. Annotate (elements or findings) in Item 60.,"<p><strong>A. </strong>Any history</p>
<p>If due to <a href=""https://www.faa.gov/ame_guide/media/Dispo_Table_Pituitary_Adenoma.pdf"" target=""_blank"" rel=""noopener"">pituitary adenoma</a> or other cause, see that page.</p>","<p><strong>Submit the following for FAA review: </strong></p>
